Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/text/util/Linkify.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
the compatibility plan's decision 6: no phone numbers are found.

Why: Linkify finds web addresses and e-mail addresses with Patterns, which framework.jar has, and phone numbers with
libphonenumber (com.android.i18n.phonenumbers), whose sources and data are not fetched. The patch drops the three
imports and lets gatherTelLinks find nothing, so TextView's autoLink and Linkify.addLinks work for web addresses and
e-mail addresses and an app that asks for phone numbers gets none, instead of a NoClassDefFoundError at the first
call. A map address needs WebView.findAddress, which the Linkify class calls unchanged.

tools/build-framework.sh applies it to a copy in build/framework/src, never to build/sources.

